      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-63595",
      ":question/problem": "Ben and Tom recorded the daily wages of seven of their co-workers. The data is given below:\n$$120, $125, $128, $130, $655, $125, $128$\n\nBen removed the outlier from the data set and computed the mean and the mean absolute deviation (MAD). Tom did the same, except he kept the outlier.\n\nWhich of the following are true statements?\n\n1. The value $$655$ is an outlier of the data set.\n2. Ben's mean value is smaller than Tom's mean value.\n3. Ben and Tom calculated the same value for the mean absolute deviation (MAD)."
